cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use OfacMatch in your work, please cite the paper below. To cite the software itself, use the metadata in this file."
title: "OfacMatch: explainable OFAC sanctions name screening"
abstract: >-
  OfacMatch screens person, company, vessel and aircraft names against the
  U.S. Treasury OFAC Specially Designated Nationals (SDN) list and explains
  every potential match, combining whole-name and name-part comparison
  (Jaro-Winkler similarity and Soundex) on OFAC's 0-100 scale. It flags
  date-of-birth and country conflicts, runs locally, and is evaluated on the
  real SDN list with a held-out test on names not used during development:
  at a threshold of 85 it finds all 4,235 realistic variations of listed
  names and 99.6% of 2,160 harder ones, and it is compared with eight
  standard name-matching methods. It is available as a .NET library, an MCP
  server for AI assistants, and a browser-based demonstration.
